<title>SPAIN: BBV to pay first interim dividend 57 ptas.</title>
<headline>BBV to pay first interim dividend 57 ptas.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's Banco Bilbao Vizcaya (BBV) said on Thursday it would pay a first interim dividend of 57 pesetas gross per share, up 21.2 percent versus the first 1996 dividend, and effective on July 19.</p>
<p>In a statement, BBV said this would represent a payment of 19 pesetas for every new share after the three-for-one share split.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
</text>
